{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST parse Rust, Python, TypeScript, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML\nsources with pinned tree-sitter grammars, selected by file extension compared\ncase-insensitively. A source with any syntax error MUST fail to parse, reporting\nthe line of its first error. Every\nother text file MUST use a plain-text profile in which each line that is not\nblank is an anonymous outline node of kind `line`. Each supported language MUST\nhave an outline profile that maps grammar node kinds to short outline kind names\nand, for each mapped kind, states whether a node is named, and by which fields\nor children, or anonymous. Only mapped kinds MUST appear in the outline; other\nnodes MUST be transparent, so their outline descendants appear under the\nnearest outline ancestor. A profile MAY attach grammar siblings to an outline\nnode, such as Rust attributes and doc comments preceding an item, so the outline\ntree need not match the grammar tree exactly; attached siblings are part of that\nnode for its line range and hash. Every file's outline MUST have a root node\nfor the whole file, independent of language. Source in no other outline node,\nsuch as top-level statements no profile maps, MUST belong to the root node;\nprofiles MUST NOT invent fallback kinds for it. Comments MUST NOT be outline nodes. Profiles MUST be\ndocumented. Upgrading a grammar or profile MAY change outlines and MUST be\ntreated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met, with true as the determination.** The implementation covers every obligation in `requirements.references.outlines`, the profiles are documented, and the tests cover the main cases and failure paths. I did not run the tests; this judgment rests on reading the sources.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Pinned grammars.**\n  - `Cargo.toml` pins every grammar with exact `=` versions: tree-sitter 0.27.1, css 0.25.0, md 0.5.4, python 0.25.0, rust 0.24.2, toml-ng 0.7.0, typescript 0.23.2 and yaml 0.7.2.\n  - `profiles()` in `src/outline/profile.rs` lists the Rust, Python, TypeScript, TSX, CSS, Markdown, TOML and YAML profiles.\n- **Extension selection.** `profile_for_path` lowercases the extension and falls back to the plain-text profile in `src/outline/plain.rs`. Paths with no extension, or an unknown one, also fall back to it.\n- **Syntax errors.**\n  - `parse_with` calls `check_errors`, which walks the tree in source order.\n  - It descends only into children that have errors and returns the first `ERROR` or `MISSING` node as an `OutlineError` carrying that node's one-based line.\n  - `OutlineCache::parse` in `src/inputs.rs` and the `outline` tool in `src/authoring/tools.rs` pass that failure on as an error.\n- **Plain text.** `plain_text` makes one anonymous `line` node for each non-blank line. A line counts as blank if it is empty after trimming, so `\\r` line endings are handled.\n- **Profile structure.**\n  - Each profile uses a `KindRule` table that maps a grammar kind to a short outline kind and a `NameRule`.\n  - The `NameRule` is `Anonymous`, `Field`, `FirstChild` or `Custom`, which covers \"named, and by which fields or children, or anonymous\".\n  - Only mapped kinds become outline nodes. `Builder::walk` recurses with the same parent for unmapped nodes, so their descendants appear under the nearest outline ancestor.\n- **Attached siblings.** The `attaches` hook attaches Rust attributes and outer doc comments, and Python decorators, to the following item. `finish` extends the node's line range to include them.\n- **Root node.** `root_node` builds a root for the whole file in every profile, with an empty kind and selector. Code that no profile maps stays with the root, and no fallback kinds are invented.\n- **Comments.** `maps` excludes comments, so they are never outline nodes. Each profile defines its own `is_comment`, and the Markdown one treats HTML comment blocks as comments.\n- **Documentation.** `md/reference.md` has an \"Outlines\" section with a full profile table, per-profile details, and a statement that grammars are pinned exactly and that upgrading one or changing a profile is a deliberate change.\n\n**Marking.** The unmarked helpers are `impl_name`, `extern_name`, `item_macro`, the Rust doc-comment helpers, and the Markdown `is_comment`. They are marked with `rust_item_selectors`, `structural_hash` or `outline_comments`, which specify that behaviour. I found no outline behaviour that lacks an `{impl}` reference.\n\n**Tests** (in `src/outline/tests.rs` and `src/authoring/tools.rs`)\n- Syntax errors: `reports_parse_failures_with_lines` covers Rust (error on line 2), Python, and TOML. For TOML it checks that the first of several errors is reported (line 3) and that the message begins `line 3:`.\n- Extension selection: `profiles_are_selected_by_extension_case_insensitively` covers uppercase extensions, no extension, and `.rs.txt`.\n- Plain text: `plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes` checks that blank lines are skipped, that nodes have kind `line`, and that a root exists.\n- Per-language profiles: Python, TypeScript and TSX, CSS, Markdown, and TOML and YAML each have their own test covering kinds, names and line ranges. These also show that comments are not nodes (Python `# lead`, CSS `/* c */`, Markdown `<!-- note -->`, TOML and YAML `# c`) and that nesting is transparent.\n- Root and fallback kinds: `file_level_inner_doc_comments_and_unmapped_code_belong_to_the_root` and `no_profile_invents_fallback_kinds` cover unmapped code, front matter, and the absence of fallback kinds across all profiles.\n- The tool-level test `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` checks the outline tool against Rust, plain-text, missing-file and denied-file inputs.\n\n**Minor gaps.**\n- Syntax-error rejection is tested for only three languages (Rust, Python, TOML). The other four reach the same shared `check_errors` code.\n- The line-range arithmetic, such as `LineIndex` and `range`, has no dedicated unit tests, but the tests above exercise it indirectly.\n\nI judged neither gap significant enough to fail the requirement.",
  "references": "9e663713c98e0a6f4aa8b020065144f361d8dfdce304ffc7fda31fcef8d4348f",
